{"id":"cmpv8v0qz000c04i96rtb90r8","description":"How about hashing in Lüneburg? There's Regiobahn every hour at :56  taking only 38 minutes from Hamburg Hbf to Lüneburg Hbf. \n\n*Hamburg H7 Hash #711* \n(seven eleven 😉)\n\n*When*: Aug. 2nd, 2 PM \n*Where*: Start in front of Lüneburg train station, on after at \"Schröders Garten\" (in good weather, 700 m from train station)\n*Trail*: About 8 k (with options to shortcut). At the end of the trail the plan is (yes, there is a plan! 😅) to jump on canoes on the river Ilmenau for an hour.\n*Hash cash*: 5 € (for the boat rental)\n\nWe'll run (or walk) through the historic city of Lüneburg with drink stop at a brewery (pay as you go). You might expect lovely views from the Kalkberg (with an old cannon on the top) and around the Kreidebergsee. \n\nBelieve it or not - Lüneburg is also famous for a \"titties bell\" as well as a \"gate to the underworld\". So, what could be a better place for hashers? 😇 Officially Lüneburg is known for its salt  production (from 9th century until 1980). More things to know or not to know about Lüneburg on Aug 2nd. 😎\n\n\"Questions?\" Let me know...\n🔛🔛 Just Period","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
