{"id":"cmr3rludc0003o2hnkpb9sdhn","description":"The Héraultics H3 and the Toulouse H3 have the privilege to hare the fabulous hangover trail for the Diva H3 Bubbly weekend in Carcassonne!\n \nThis sparkling trail will (probably?) take you through the lanes of the mediaval city, looking for Blanquette de Limoux, the local bubbly! Also this occasion to discover a fantastic group of Divas, Toyboys and SuggarDaddies!\n\nPlease RSVP if you plan on joining the Diva H3 on that hangover trail.\n\nWhen : Sunday April 19th at 10:00, for first tasting and chalk-talk at 10:30\n\nWhere :  meeting in front of the Tribe Hotel, 2 rue des 3 couronnes in Carcassonne\n\nOn-After : Finish the bubbles and go visit the town","street":"2 Rue des Trois Couronnés, 11000","cost":"€10","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rlui30005o2hnsl5478fo","description":"Please join us us on Sunday 24th May.\n\nWHEN:\nSunday 24 may at 3pm. Please arrive 15 minutes early to ensure a timely start.\n\nWHERE:\nhttps://maps.app.goo.gl/TxVqE9QgJXn4UEDv8?g_st=ic\n\nWHAT TO BRING:\nWater, a drinking beaker, 5€ hash cash, plus 12€ for your t-shirt if you don’t already have it \n\nHoping to see you there! Please let us know if you intend to cum for provisions planning (aka beer 😋)\n\nOn on,\nDicken Cider & E.T","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rlumf0007o2hne28670c2","description":"Souls,\n\nPlease be invited to the Toulouse H3 Run #293 hared by GH & Fly By Night\n\nThe start location is Parking du Parc de Gagnac, Gagnac-sur-Garonne, see link below\nhttps://maps.app.goo.gl/YzsGXECvJ9mJNkwS9\n\nTrail starts at 15h but please arrive no later than 14h45 for the admin and briefing\n\nPlease remember to bring with you:\n- Plenty of water, it could be hot\n- Sun screen, there are many sections without shade\n- Head protection, for the same reasons\n- Your drinking vessel\n- 5€ (+12€ if you still need to buy the t-shirt)\n- Your hash gear, or risk down-downs later on\n\nDo not bring\n- Animals\nOr understand that animals will not be allowed at the beer stop\n\nPlease let me know via here, whats app, carrier pigeon, etc (if not done already) if you plan to come\n\nFor those of you in the centre of Toulouse, I trust you will coordinate together about ride sharing\n\nOn On!\n\nGH & FBN","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rt4xf0001yvhnoe7kzzqm","description":"*Make sure you check in or you might not get run credit*\n\nIf you are now registered with Harrier Central you can register own attendance via app by scanning QR code  that will be available at run start. This will be a test!\n\n\nHare:\nEric the ***\n\nOn Inn:\nCharwoods\n47 Buckstone Terrace  \nFairmilehead\nEH10 6QJ\n\nCoronavirus:\nPlease be aware that the virus is still with us and continue to check and adhere to latest restrictions and advice from the Scottish Government here. https://www.gov.scot/coronavirus-covid-19/\nDo not attend if you feel unwell and (do we even need to say this?) if you test positive.\nMask wearing regulations were withdrawn on 18th April but with case again rising use of masks may be sensible  in indoor spaces while remaining a matter of personal irresponsibility.\n\nBuses:\n11, 15. Please be guided by the Transport for Edinburgh smartphone app or the website below to find the best route for you.\n\nSee also the TNTH3 website: https://tnth3.teamapp.com/","street":"47 Buckstone Terrace, EH10 6QJ","cost":"£1","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rt51v0003yvhn8abst3jv","description":"*Make sure you check in or you might not get a run credit*\n\nHares:\nHairspray\nRugrat\n\nOn Inn:\nThe Harbour Inn\n4-6 Fishmarket Square \nNewhaven \nEH6 4LW\n\nCoronavirus:\nPlease be aware that the virus is still with us and continue to check and adhere to latest restrictions and advice from the Scottish Government here. https://www.gov.scot/coronavirus-covid-19/\nDo not attend if you feel unwell and (do we even need to say this?) if you test positive.\nMask wearing regulations were withdrawn from 18th April but are again suggested in confined spaces and are a matter of personal irresponsibility.\n\nBuses:\n11, 16, and 7.  Please be guided by the Transport for Edinburgh smartphone app or the website below to find the best route for you.\nhttps://lothianbuses.co.uk/getting-around/journey-planner\n\nSee also the TNTH3 website: https://tnth3.teamapp.com/","street":"Fishmarket square,Newhaven","cost":"£1","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rt56a0005yvhnfskxg2s7","description":"Make sure you check in or you might not get a run credit. \n\nHares:\nSimon the Basta*rd (Duke of Edinburgh)\n\nOn Inn:\nPortobello Tap\n87 Portobello High Street\nEH15 1AW\n\nHarrier Central Users:\nWhen you get to the run venue, open the app and  a box will appear saying “Are you joining TNT on Run No. ????”; by tickinmg the YES box, this will update your run count.  If you forget, go into \"History\" at the bottom of the page (3 dots, 3 lines) on the right hand side, click on your hash run count, click on the 3 dots beside the appropriate Run No. However please note that the Hare Raiser is always right. and OnSec is only uploading run history as and when a new app user is identified.\n\nCoronavirus:\nPlease be aware that the virus is still with us and continue to check and adhere to latest restrictions and advice from the Scottish Government here. https://www.gov.scot/coronavirus-covid-19/\nDo not attend if you feel unwell and (do we even need to say this?) if you test positive.\nMask wearing regulations were withdrawn from 18th April but are again suggested in confined spaces and are a matter of personal irresponsibility.\n\nBuses:\nPlease be guided by the Transport for Edinburgh smartphone app or the website below to find the best route for you.\nhttps://lothianbuses.co.uk/getting-around/journey-planner","street":"87 Portobello High Street, EH15 1AW","cost":"£1","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rt5aw0007yvhnol8tze9v","description":"NOTE CHANGE OF ON INN\nMake sure you check in or you might not get a run credit. \n\nHares:\nTongue Lasher\nSniffer Dog\n\nOn Inn:\nBennets of Morningside\n1 Maxwell Street \nEH10 5HT\n\nHarrier Central Users:\nWhen you get to the run venue, open the app and  a box will appear saying “Are you joining TNT on Run No. ????”; by ticking the YES box, this will update your run count.  If you forget, go into \"History\" at the bottom of the page (3 dots, 3 lines) on the right hand side, click on your hash run count, click on the 3 dots beside the appropriate Run No. However please note that the Hare Raiser is always right. and OnSec is only uploading run history as and when a new app user is identified.\n\nCoronavirus:\nPlease be aware that the virus is still with us and continue to check and adhere to latest restrictions and advice from the Scottish Government here. https://www.gov.scot/coronavirus-covid-19/\nDo not attend if you feel unwell and (do we even need to say this?) if you test positive.\nMask wearing regulations were withdrawn from 18th April but are again suggested in confined spaces and are a matter of personal irresponsibility.\n\nBuses:\nMany. Please be guided by the Transport for Edinburgh smartphone app or the website below to find the best route for you.\nhttps://lothianbuses.co.uk/getting-around/journey-planner","street":"1 Maxwell St","cost":"£1","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
