{"id":"cmr3rt6zg000xyvhnmw92qkbn","description":"Make sure you check in and pay or you might not get a run credit. \n\nThis is AGM run also tallying with Big Mac's birth year. Please support your hash and a new and exciting venue. Best be there to avoid getting voted on to Mismanagement Committee.\n\nHares:\nBig Mac\nFleshmob\n\nOn Inn:\nNewbarns Brewery Taproom\n13 Jane Street \nLeith\nEH6 5HE\n\n(This is just off Leith Walk near the Foot)\n///agents.advice.elaborate\n\nHarrier Central Users:\nWhen you get to the run venue, open the app and  a box will appear saying “Are you joining TNT on Run No. ????”; by ticking the YES box, this will update your run count.  If you forget, go into \"History\" at the bottom of the page (3 dots, 3 lines) on the right hand side, click on your hash run count, click on the 3 dots beside the appropriate Run No. However please note that the Hare Raiser is always right. and OnSec is only uploading run history as and when a new app user is identified.\n\nCoronavirus:\nPlease be aware that the virus is still with us and continue to check and adhere to latest restrictions and advice from the Scottish Government here. https://www.gov.scot/coronavirus-covid-19/\nDo not attend if you feel unwell and (do we even need to say this?) if you test positive.\nMask wearing regulations were withdrawn from 18th April but are again suggested in confined spaces and are a matter of personal irresponsibility.\n\nBuses:\nMany buses serve the Kirkgate at present Jane Street is a 5 minute walk from ther Foot on right hand side and inconspicuous brewery is on left about 30m from junction. Returning into town is straightforward as buses are heading up Leith Walk.  Please be guided by the Transport for Edinburgh smartphone app or the website below to find the best route for you.\nhttps://lothianbuses.co.uk/getting-around/journey-planner","street":"5 Jane Street, EH6 5HD, EH6 5HE","cost":"£1","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
