{"id":"cmr3ruknb00031jhnceddvadn","description":"Next full moon is upon us, and time for another fun run in Leiden. Bring your flashlights/torches and come for some fun running! The beer is cold, and perhaps if spring turns back into winter, we will arrange warm drinks!\n\nThe start is in front of the Mercedes dealer behind the station. Less than 10min walk, and you'll see the car parked there somewhere.\n\nHare: Opee\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rukru00051jhnmoo693qy","description":"The full moon is upon us, and it's time to head back to The Hague. To mix things up, we even have a new hare--FILTH newcomer Boerskin. The intense rains and winds seem to be behind us, so grab your flashlights/torches and join us for some fun running! \n\nThe hare is kind enough to allow us to invade his home so we have somewhere to drop our bags and to warm up afterwards. There lots of free street parking in front of the house. Public transport: from Den Haag Centraal, take Tram 9 direction Scheveningen, get off at the Javabrug stop and then walk 300m.\n\nHare: Boerskin\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!","street":"24A Bachmanstraat, 2596JC","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rukwy00071jhnfzdn18wd","description":"NOTE 1: We have 3 start times to allow people working in AMS ample time to get to the run and then enjoy the Beach festival with us!\n\nNOTE 2: Opee is offering crash space to anyone that wants to chill at the beach late and then return to AMS the next morning.\n\n=======\n\nDETAILS\n\nIt's hard to believe that one of the best places to chill is on the beach in front of a bonfire, but trust me, it's hard to find a place to be more relaxed.\n\nJoin me and other FILTH Hashers at this year's Bonfire Beach Festival at Scheveningen Beach. First runners off at 19:30, but there will be options to join the run at 20:00 and 20:30 as well. The end will be at the Bonfire Beach Festival where we will spend the next 3-4 hours hanging out on the beach, drinking wine and watching the long slow sunset.\n\nWe will have some beer for down-downs, but we plan to go to a local store immediately after the run so we can each purchase wine, cheese and other snacks for our chill to time on the beach.\n\nHope to see you there...  VIRGINS welcome! :-)\n\nOnOn! \nOpee\n\n========== Details ==========\n\nRun #: 146\nTheme: Bonfire Beach Festival\nDate: Friday, 19 Apr\nTime: 19:30\nLocation: Scheveningen Beach Pier (where the pier meets the boardwalk)\nBag Drop: Yes (and bring a beach blanket too!)\nHash cash: €5.00\nRSVP: Yes, please! On Facebook or send e-mail to [redacted]\n\nNOTE: If you want to join us later because you are unable to get to the beach by 19:30, no problem. You will be able to join the trail at 20:00 and 20:30 as well. We cater to all needs!","street":"Strandweg 152, 2586JW","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rul1u00091jhnip6a7n1r","description":"(NOTE: If you cannot make 10:30, but still want to join for brunch, see the note at the end of the post)\n\nAfter an intense few days partying in The Hague for King's Night and then partying with H4 in The Hague or in Amsterdam for King's Day, what better way to recover than to run with the FILTH Hash in Leiden!\n\nWe'll start at the Leiden train station (lockers are available) and make our way through the lovely Leiden canals on a short(ish) run that will end in a city park where we will have a champagne brunch complete with delicious baked goods, fruit, eggs and juices.\n\nFirst you'll party like a King, then Hash like a King and then you'll eat like a King!\n\nRSVP REQUIRED:  No RSVP, means you will be at the end of the food line and we won't be able to guarantee there will be enough. Please RSVP to: [redacted] or by SMS'ing [redacted].\n\nHope to see you there!\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee\n\nNote: we are timing this run so that people from Brussels will have the opportunity to run, eat and get back to BXL for the BMPH3 AGM.\n\n==============\n\nDetails:\nRun number: n/a (this is a FILTH non-numbered event)\nDate: 28 Apr\nTime: 10:30 pack off\nLocation: Leiden Central Station, exit on the city side\nHares: Give it a Blow & Opee\nRun fee: €5 + €5 if you want brunch\nRSVP: Required if you want us to hold food for you\nBag drop: Yes, lockers are available at the station\n\nNOTE for latecomers: If you think you will be late, please let me know and I will connect you into the WhatsApp group we are setting up for the run. We will then allow you to live track the hares and join the trail in progress or meet us at the end.","street":"Stationsplein 3, 2312 AJ","cost":"€10","clear_run":147,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rul6b000b1jhn30fuyypc","description":"Let's get FILTHY with Patti!\n\nCome and celebrate Patti's 40th birthday in true Hash style... with lots of beer, partying (and maybe some other intoxicants).\n\nThe fun starts at the classic Genever bar, Wyland Fockink in Amsterdam. We will then do a running pub crawl to at least 3 other different venues. At any point, you can switch from the FILTH runner's trail to the walker's trail if you decide you've logged enough kilometers.\n\nBEWARE: There is NO bag drop. So please travel light! There will be walkers if you want to find someone to carry some small personal items for you.\n\nHope to see you all there!\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee\n\n======= DETAILS =======\n\nRun #: FILTH #147\nDate: SATURDAY, May 18th\nTime: 19:00\nLocation: Wyland Fockink, Amsterdam\nRun fee: €5.00\nBag drop: NO... please carry what you bring or find a willing friend\nRSVP: Yes, to this FB event or to [redacted]\nTheme: Patti's 40th Birthday Bash!","street":"Pijlsteeg 31, 1012 HH","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulbb000d1jhnu4u56umj","description":"Meet next to the Mercedes Dealer 'behind' the station. Exit city side, walk right past all the bikes, past the first bridge, then turn right under the second bridge. You should see us on the left. Or user the map pin.\nHare: Tasty Piss\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"vondellaan 45, 2332 aa","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulg7000f1jhn3w1010mm","description":"It is with great sadness that we will soon be bidding farewell to Strobe My Balls, who was named at the FILTH in 2016. He has embraced being a Dutch hasher all the way down to his wooden shoes. Don't miss your chance to hash on his last sh*tty FILTH trail. He promises a happy ending for all who make the trip out to Utrecht.\n\n======== Details ========\nTime: 19:30\nDate: Friday 19 July\nHare: Strobe My Balls\nLocation: Oudegracht 279, Utrecht\nA to A*\nBag drop: Yes\nHash cash: €5","street":"279 Oudegracht, 3511PA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulkn000h1jhnmjr15q67","description":"Meet in the parking lot of \"De Stal\" opposite the Naturalis Museum. Very short walk from the station.\n\nHash Cash: €5\nHare: Tasty Piss\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Darwinweg 1","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruloy000j1jhnh9x66a6m","description":"A wonderful trail, followed by a BBQ in Overveen, and potentially swimming if the RA does a good job! :-)\n\nLocation: Overveen train station\nHare: Give it a Blow & Start Me Up\nBag Drop: Yes\nA-B run (bag drop will move)\nHash Cash: €10","street":"Tetterodeweg 2","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rultu000l1jhnjjr8jd14","description":"The FILTH is celebrating Canadian HashGiving this year with The Hague H3 by starting at the same location that they will be having an earlier hash. You're welcome to come for one or both. See below for the separate registration for The Hague's special hash, which includes dinner for the early birds.  \n\n======== Details ========\nWhen: Sunday 13 October at 19:30\nHare: Do Me Moore + Joe Dirt\nLocation: Hoornbruglaan 47, 2281 AV Rijswijk, Nederland\nBag drop: Yes\nHash cash: €5\n\nThere will be a The Hague Hash run right before, at 14:00, so join both!\n\nRSVP: register for this event on The Hague H3 website:\nhttps://www.haguehash.nl/thanksgiving\nThe Moore Dirts are providing food for the first 30 people. More than 30 hashers are always welcome, but they will have to order pizza or something at their own expense. \n\nHares: Joe Dirt and Do Me Moore\nWhen: Sunday October 13th at 14:00 hrs\nWhere: Chez Moore Dirt, Hoornbruglaan 47, 2281 AV Rijswijk\nGood to know: Bring Your Own Drinks for Dinner\nHash cash: €5\n\nJoe Dirt and Do Me Moore are planning once again to host HashThanksGiving. However, this year they are traveling back stateside for actual American Thanksgiving. So they are haring HashGiving around Canadian ThanksGiving on Sunday 13 October (yes indeed, one whole day before the Canadian Thanksgiving and a whopping 46 days before the real one)\n\nThere will be the now traditional picture run at 14:00 with the meal to follow. The meal will be free for the first 30 people to fill out the form and commit to bringing your own drinks for dinner.\n\nThen at 19:30 there will be the October FILTH run at the same location. This means two hashes & two circles & two times hash cash (you are getting twice the beer).","street":"47 Hoornbruglaan, 2281AV","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rulz4000n1jhn7a8uhdk0","description":"World leaders don't seem to be making much progress with diplomacy... there HAS to be a better way. Well, we think there is and it's BEER. Join us at the Hague Humanity Hub in The Hague where we will explore what it means to make Peace with bottles in our hands.\n\nHope to see you all there! Bring friends and virgins so we can have even more peace!\n\n====== Details ======\n\nRun #: n/a\nTheme: World Piece Through Beer\nDate: Thur 24 Oct\nTime: 19:00 gather / 19:15 pack off\nBag Drop: Yes\nRun Fee: €5.00","street":"58 Fluwelen Burgwal, 2511CJ","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rum41000p1jhnpj7kguot","description":"FILTH 154 will be on Monday 11 November! Double time to celebrate, as it's the start of carnival, and we will celebrate South Africa's World Cup victory. So either dress up as something worthy of carnival, or wear green and gold, OR BOTH!\n\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes, the Pub\nHare: Boar Whore","street":"oude singel 2, 2312RA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rum8e000r1jhnkl0dvpy3","description":"Whilst the UK is taken over by Election Fever and School Nativity Plays are being disrupted, we'll have a hash under the light of the December Cold Full Moon. First results could be coming in as circle is drawing to a close.. Spannend!\n\nLocation : Chez Edge\nDag Drop : Yes\nHash Cash : 5 euro or £5\nHare : On The Edge","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumcw000t1jhn2ww1k68t","description":"Some hashers are visiting from Brussels, so we decided to do an impromptu New Year's Hangover Run on Wednesday. Starting at Chez Tasty Boar!\n\nAll are welcome!\n\nTime: 11:30 AM\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!\nHare: Opee","street":"196 Diamantlaan, 2332GR","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumh7000v1jhn4vziukcm","description":"January FILTH, hosted by Semen Spirit!\n\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Chez Semen Spirit\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"37 Gillis van Ledenberchstraat, 1052TZ","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumll000x1jhnf4ogvnru","description":"Time for some fun in the suburbs of Leiden while trying to stay upright during the strong winds of Tropical Storm Ciara.\n\nHare: Tasty Piss\nHash Cash: €5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"196 Diamantlaan, 2332GR","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumqi000z1jhnv06glk9a","description":"Time for a great Monday-night run around Hoofddorp for the March Full Moon!\n\nEasy single train from Amsterdam, so enough time for your beauty sleep afterwards!\n\nGreat opportunity to end Monday blues with Monday Beers!\n\nHare: Tasty Piss\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!\nBeer: Yes!\nFull Moon: Yes!","street":"Hoofddorp, 2132 HA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumv800111jhngkh07iin","description":"Since we can't run outside in groups, we will do a virtual FILTH run. Similar to other runs we've been doing with other hashers, you run your own trail, and then join circle.\n\nFollow the guidelines below, and your run will be counted as a FILTH run:\n- You must run on 8 April 2020 (Full Moon)\n- You must post evidence of your trail, with a photo in this event. Preferably a GPS track of your trail, so you can comply with guideline 1.\n- This is the FILTH, we are ambitious, so trail has ru.. guidelines:\n1. Trail must be minimum 5km long\n2. Trail must include the full moon (send a photo, doesn't matter if the clouds block it.)\n- Join the circle at 21:00 via Zoom (Link will be posted in the event)","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rumzz00131jhnf8rx8jfs","description":"Time for another Full Moon, and yes, we're still locked down!\n\nIt's simple, you run your own trail, and then join circle.\nFollow the guidelines below, and your run will be counted as a FILTH run:\n- You must run on 7 May 2020 (Full Moon)\n- You must post evidence of your trail, with a photo in this event. Preferably a GPS track of your trail, so you can comply with guideline 1.\n- This is the FILTH, we are ambitious, so trail has ru.. guidelines:\n1. Trail must be minimum 5km long\n2. Trail must include the full moon (send a photo, doesn't matter if the clouds or the earth or something blocks it.)\n- Join the circle at 21:00 via Zoom (Link will be posted in the event)","street":"43 Langebrug, 2311TH","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3run4u00151jhntlbnvfx6","description":"We will be running in the dunes in Wassenaar! Tasty will be giving us a wonderful trail, and Tuna will ensure an hour or 2 of dry weather!\n\nIt seems we are not expecting people coming by public transport, so this evening will mean you have to come by car and bike. Please let us know if that's a problem and we can see what assistance can be given (though I'm not hopeful).\n\nWe will follow all necessary social distancing rules, but we will have a circle, a real one!","street":"Katwijkseweg 2, 2242 PA","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3run9a00171jhngvc6w4qv","description":"This month's full moon happens to fall on a Sunday, so the FILTH H3 and Amsterdam H3 are joining forces for a special hash in Leiden. If the Hash Gods are kind, we will have a floating beer stop. \n\nPublic transport can now be used for non-essential trips--just don't forget your mask. There are direct trains from Amsterdam Centraal, Amsterdam Zuid and Den Haag Centraal to Leiden Centraal. The start is a 10-minute walk from the station. \n\nDETAILS\n\nDate: Sunday 5 July\nTime: 15:00\nHare: Opee + Boar Whore\nLocation: In front of Duke of Oz at Oude Singel 2, 2312 RA Leiden\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes\nBring: Your own mug and snacks","street":"2 Oude Singel, 2312RA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rundv00191jhnrgm6zqco","description":"The August Full Moon has snuck up on us with several of our regular hashers having other plans (like f*@king off to Spain or taking care of a newborn), so we're going to try something different: a pub crawl during a pandemic. Of course, that means staying socially distanced while drinking together at random bars on their outdoor terraces. This will be a live lay with Opee making it up as he goes. So only a runners trail will be laid, while walkers will receive instructions on how to get to the next stop. Are you up to the challenge?\n\nDETAILS\nDate: Monday 3 August\nTime: 19:00\nHare: Opee \nLocation: In front of Leiden Centraal Station\nHash cash: € 0\nBag drop: No, although you should be able to rent a locker at the station\nBRING CASH for pay-as-you-go pub crawl","street":"Stationsplein 3-B, 2312 AJ","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3runib001b1jhnb2nlv6x5","description":"It's that time of the month again, and since we have been slacking, it's a last-minute hare and location decision.\nBoar Whore (yours truly) will set a wonderful live trail, not too long (legs tired) and will end with great beer!\n\nHash cash as usual, €5, and bag drop at our place in Leiden.\n\nONON!","street":"196 Diamantlaan, 2332 GR","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3runmh001d1jhn1w2nsous","description":"It's that time of the month again, and since our usual hares have been working their butts off lately, it's once again a last-minute announcement. \n\nIn fact, everything about this will be so last minute, that our hare will literally be making it up as he goes, thus there will be no official walker's trail. \n\nBring money on trail just in case we manage to stop by some pubs. Also bring a flashlight as we'll be starting at sunset. \n\nPlease note that we will be following the latest government guidelines and keeping our distance while remaining outside.\n\nFree parking is available at the station.\n\n********************************************\nDETAILS:\nDate: Friday 2 October 2020\nGather Time: 19:15 Pack Off: 19:30\nHares: Opee\nLocation: Voorschoten Station\nHash cash: € 5\nBag Drop: Can be arranged","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3runrl001f1jhnt117alxa","description":"Since our plan to host a socially distanced pub crawl to celebrate this annual global hashing event has been locked down, here's your chance to do your very own Virtual All-You-Can-Drink Pub Crawl with as many beer stops at your own house as you feel like having. \n\nJust like past virtual hashes, you run your own trail, and then join circle. \n\nThis is the FILTH--we are ambitious--so trail has ru.. guidelines in order for your run to be counted:\n1. You must run on 24 October 2020 (World Peace Through Beer Day)\n2. Trail must be minimum of 5km (post proof such as a GPS track)\n3. Trail must include the full moon (post a photo in the event, doesn't matter if clouds, Earth or something else blocks it)\n4. Beer stop should include good beer (send a photo to prove that you're not just drinking crap beer)\n5. Join the circle at 21:00 via Zoom (Link will be posted in the event)","street":"22 Prins Bernhardstraat, 2215 AW","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3runw7001h1jhn41a6t6l6","description":"In a rare cosmic convergence, not only is this Saturday the Full Hunter Moon, but it is also a Blue Moon (2nd full moon this month) and Halloween. What better thing to do to celebrate, but to hash?\n\nSadly, our plans to host a joint Halloween Hash with AH3, complete with a spooky tour of Amsterdam's haunted properties and homebrewed pumpkin beer courtesy of Missing Link, were thwarted by corona restrictions. However, that shouldn't stop us from putting on our costumes, grabbing a hash buddy or two and joining the FILTH for our first (and hopefully only) Virtual Halloween Hash. \n\nThis is the FILTH--we are ambitious--so trail has ru.. guidelines in order for your run to be counted:\n\n1. You must run on 31 October 2020 (preferably in a Halloween costume)\n2. Trail must be minimum of 5km (post proof such as a GPS track)\n3. Trail must include the full moon (post a photo in the event, doesn't matter if clouds, Earth or something else blocks it)\n4. Beer stop should include good beer (send a photo to prove that you're not just drinking crap beer)\n5. Join the circle at 21:00 via Zoom (Link will be posted in the event)","street":"22 Prins Bernhardstraat, 2215 AW","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruo0l001j1jhnadkk0eqw","description":"Although the Full Beaver Moon isn't actually until Monday 30 November, it just happens that our hare will already be in Amsterdam on the 29th and hopefully hashers will be available to try something new with us: a Hybrid Hash.\n\nRemember how we used to be able to gather together in one big socially distanced group? Not sure when that will be possible again, but let's try to make the best of it by gathering in multiple groups of up to four to enjoy another live lay by Opee (who's busy plotting how to  have a beer break on trail). Rather than the usual festivities at the end of trail with beer and munchies, we will each get one beer and can then f*&k off or stay to chat in groups of up to four. A link for a virtual circle will be posted later. \n\nPlease note that we will be following the latest government guidelines and keeping our distance while remaining outside. It will be chilly and there won't be a bag drop, so please plan accordingly.\n********************************************\nDETAILS:\nDate: Sunday 29 November 2020\nGather Time: 14:00 Pack Off: 14:15\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Haarlemmerpoort, Haarlemmerplein, Amsterdam\nHash cash: Free (courtesy of AH3)\nBag Drop: No (Sorry!)","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruo4v001l1jhnzoz6z3f2","description":"Lockdown is still in effect, but the moon is still full, and running and drinking will still happen!\n\nSo go out for a run tomorrow (29 December), make it FILTHy (proper distance, or something to make it worthy of a decent hash!) and show up for circle! No run, no fun!\n\nCircle details will be shared tomorrow, and it will start at 20:00 (that's 8pm Leiden time!)\n\nOnOn!!!","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruo9m001n1jhnj9qsxcen","description":"Although lockdown has been extended into the New Year, the moon will still be full, so running and drinking will still happen!\n\nSo go out for a run on Thursday (28 January), make it FILTHy (proper distance, or something to make it worthy of a decent hash) and show up for circle at 21:00 (a good excuse not to break curfew). No run, no fun!\n\nCircle details will be shared via email (please send your email address to Tasty or Boar Whore). A laptop is required for this unique circle experience and space is limited.\nOnOn!!","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruody001p1jhn3fcoyypb","description":"Another virtual hash with a Zoom circle afterwards, although Tasty Piss will actually lay trail in Leiden/Valkenburg/Rijnburg.","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruoib001r1jhn9snu1kvc","description":"Although lockdown has been extended yet again, spring is finally here and the moon will still be full, so running and drinking will still happen!\n\nSo go out for a run on Sunday (28 March), make it FILTHy (proper distance, or something to make it worthy of a decent hash) and show up for circle at 21:00. No run, no fun!\n\nCircle details will be shared on Sunday.","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruomm001t1jhnylwonqxo","description":"Are you?\n\nKoningsnacht (King’s Night) is coming up and in a normal year we would go out partying in The Hague… but this year is a bit different. Does that mean we can’t party… NO! We’ll just party different in 2021!\n\nThis year AH3 is throwing an online dance party with an open bar* that will keep you moving until the wee hours of the morning.\n\nTo join, it’s best to have two devices:\nAudio: Use any mobile phone or other device that can be easily connected to a Bluetooth speaker or other external speaker and tune into the audio stream using this link:\n\nhttps://bit.ly/dance-a\n\nVideo: Using a laptop, tablet or computer with a video camera tune into the video stream which will be on Zoom where we can see each other dancing (don’t forget to mute your audio on Zoom). It’s best to set Zoom on “tile mode” where you can see a lot of people on one screen. To tune into the video, use the following link:\n\nhttps://bit.ly/dance-v\n\nThe party starts at 1900 (7PM) and will go until we turn the disco lights off (usually around 3AM or 4AM in the morning!).\n\nWe hope you find the time to tune in and join in the fun!\n\nCheers!\n\nOpee & Tuna","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":175,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruorj001v1jhno1p1new4","description":"FULL MOON time again!\nTomorrow it might be the king's birthday, but that's of course not the most important thing. Much more important is that the moon will be at it's fullest glory again. So it's time for a run.\n\nStill in lockdown, so do your own running thing, then join us after for circle at 19:00. Link will be posted.\n\nOnOn!","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruow1001x1jhnzx1ml7qw","description":"Eurovision is coming to Holland! Perhaps you're excited and plan to watch it.…or perhaps you're like us and will be happy to find another way to listen to music that night.\n\nIn honor of Eurovision, Amsterdam H3 is throwing an online dance party with an open bar* that will keep you moving until the wee hours of the morning.\n\nTo join, it’s best to have two devices:\nAudio: Use any mobile phone or other device that can be easily connected to a Bluetooth speaker or other external speaker and tune into the audio stream using this link:\n\nhttps://bit.ly/hash-a\n\nVideo: Using a laptop, tablet or computer with a video camera tune into the video stream which will be on Zoom where we can see each other dancing (don’t forget to mute your audio). It’s best to set Zoom on “tile mode” where you can see a lot of people on one screen. To tune into the video, use this link:\n\nhttps://bit.ly/hash-v2\n\nThe party starts at 20:00 (8PM) and will go until we turn the disco lights off (usually around 3AM or 4AM in the morning!).\n\nWe hope you find the time to tune in and join in the fun!\n\nOn-On!\nDJ Opee\n\n*For free booze, open your liquor cabinet and enjoy.","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":175,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rup07001z1jhnnt0ikfe7","description":"Join us IN-PERSON for the next FILTH run starting in Leiden (about 15 minute walk from Leiden Centraal). Help us turn May's Flower Full Moon into a Flour Full Moon. Let's get our legs and our tongue's back in shape after a long pause from Hashing in-person.\n*******************************\nTime: Wednesday 26 May at 19:15\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Maresingel 56, 2316 HE Leiden\nHash cash: € 5 \nBag drop: Yes","street":"56 Maresingel, 2316 HE","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rup4500211jhn1judnvk7","description":"It's SUMMER! (Took long enough!)... and time for a summer \"beer crawl\" in Leiden. This will be a trail for both runners and walkers. Walkers will go directly from beer to beer and runners will take a more circuitous route. :-). Expect 3-4k for walkers, 8-10k for runners. (Note: walkers, bring a picnic blanket so you can hang out at the beer breaks).\n\nCome on out and enjoy the nice weather and good drinks... I promise to bring you only the finest beers available in Leiden  plus lots of other good sightseeing for the runners.\n\nAs it's summer and a beer crawl there will be no bag drop - travel light and hand stuff you have that you don't want to run with to a willing walker for transport from beer to beer.\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee","street":"2 Oude Singel, 2312 RA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rup8n00231jhn2o4tvrw6","description":"It's time to celebrate the first Dutch kid in space! If you haven't noticed, there's a space war taking place amongst billionaires. For us poor hashers, it's an excuse to get spacy (meaning tinfoil hats, of course). \n********************************************\nTime: Friday 23 July at 19:30\nHare: Tasty Piss\nLocation: Morsstraat 24, 2312 BM Leiden\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: No","street":"Morsstraat 24, 2312 BM","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rupd200251jhnv2y731d4","description":"Most of our regular FILTH hashers will likely be nursing quite a hangover after partying for days at Eurohash in Prague, so let's gather together at the hash dorm and run a Hangover Hash. \n\nIn a twist of fate, another hash was planned for the same time and now we’ve combined efforts. Not one, but two hares extraordinare, Hazekasi and Opee will join efforts to live Kay the trail. It will be too complicated to collect hash cash, so plan on bringing cash on trail for beer stops. Of course, feel free to invite your old and new friends as this trail will be open to all runners. If there's interest in a walker's trail, someone will need to volunteer to lay that trail.\n\n********************************************\nTime: Sunday 22 August at 10:00 (NOTE NEW TIME)\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Hash Dorm in Prague\nBring cash for beer stops","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruphk00271jhnbhdc757k","description":"It's hard to believe but it's already been a year since we've hashed from Boar Whore and Tasty's place in Leiden. It's Boar Whore's turn to lay a live trail. As always, he promises a good trail with great beer at the end. Keep an eye out for hungry ghosts on our first hash in the dark in months. \n\n********************************************\nTime: Monday 20 September at 19:30\nHare: Boar Whore\nLocation: Diamantlaan 196, 2332 GR Leiden\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"196 Diamantlaan, 2332 GR","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruplz00291jhn1od5puy6","description":"It's been two years since we've been able to celebrate World Peace Through Beer Day and what better way than with a pub crawl! Join us at the Hague Humanity Hub in The Hague where we will explore what it means to make Peace with bottles in our hands. Don't forget to bring cash or a debit card on trail. \n\nBring friends and virgins so we can have even more Peace!\n\n********************************************\nTime: Wednesday 20 October at 19:00\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Hague Humanity Hub\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"58 Fluwelen Burgwal, 2511 CJ","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rupqe002b1jhnbfj0xi98","description":"Hares: Opee, Give it a Blow and scary zombies!\n\nTrail start: Borgoumont 83, 4987 Stoumont, Belgium\n\nHow to get there:\nCar is best option - car pool with your zombie friends.\n\nPublic transport: Coo train station is approximately 8km from trail start. Hashers with cars can shuttle between train station and trail start if required. We'll make arrangements closer to the time. \n\nWhere to stay overnight: \nCoo is only 9km away and closest place to stay over Saturday night. Spa is approximately 14km away. \n\nSome hashers have booked to stay here: \n\nLe Coffee Ride Cycling Cafe: https://www.lecoffeeride.cc/ \nAu Sommet de la Cascade: https://ausommetdelacascade.eatbu.com/?lang=en\n\nHangover trail: Opee will hare a \"shiggirific\" hangover trail on Sunday morning with beautiful views of the three rivers along with a visit to Belgium's tallest waterfall. Don't miss this amazing weekend experience in the Ardennes!\n\nOther info: Details are also available on the fantastic Harrier Central app!\n\nOnOn!\nOpee and Give it a Blow","street":"83 Borgoumont, 4987","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rupv7002d1jhnmq7x1zlh","description":"If you still have any brains left after having them eaten by the zombies, join us for this nice hangover run in the beautiful Woods around Coo","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rupz4002f1jhnepwug4bp","description":"After careful consideration, it's come to the hares' attention that it is no longer summer. However, that won't stop Swaffelaar from daring to be devirginized by Opee on what is likely to be our final weekend this year of double digits. We will definitely be venturing outside of the city streets, so don't forget a headlamp or flashlight. \n\n------\n\nDetails:\n\nLocation: Leiden Central Station (LUMC side)\nDate: Friday 19 November\nTime: 19:30\nHares: Swaffelaar (virgin lay!) and Opee\nBag drop: Yes\nTheme: Anything you can think of that will warm you up\nHash cash: €5\n\n\nSee you there!\n\nOn-On!\n\nOpee","street":"Stationsplein 3-B, 2312 AJ","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruq36002h1jhnwsx9itsl","description":"Join us for the last-minute \"pull it oudda butt\" hash in Leiden. For those coming by public transit, this will be an A-to-B hash starting at the back side of the station and ending where we can circle up without a crowd. If you are driving, go directly to the B-point at Leidse Hout where cars will be parked and bags will be dropped (NOTE: The map on FB and Harrier Central for this run shows you where the B location is). Don’t forget your head torch and something warm to wear at the socially-distanced end. Was a great run!","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruq7j002j1jhn0jg1qy2h","description":"It's time to stop talking about it and finally do it: let's start hashing on the Saturday closest to the new moon! And what better way to celebrate the new moon than to experience the Utrecht Lumen route. Walkers will follow the offical 3K route while runners will follow Opee's trail. Both should have plenty of opportunities to grab a drink and a bite along the way. Don't forget your Coronapass!\n\n*************************************\nTime: Saturday 29 January at 18:00 \nHare: Opee\nLocation: Utrecht Station (exit towards city center and meet near Five Guys Burger restaurant) Harrier Central pin is on the exact location. \nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Lockers available at station","street":"305 Stationshal, 3511 CE","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqbt002l1jhnzqrzd7u5","description":"UPDATE: Exact location of bag drop will be here:\nSchenkkade 256, 2595 AW Den Haag, Netherlands close to the Laan van NOI station. \n\nHarrier Central app has precise pin location for the run start which is at the station. \n\n=======\n\nFebruary's Full Moon is just HOURS away and SPRING is in the air! Come and Hash with us on Wednesday, Feb 16th for a nice run where I will try to find some VIRGIN territory in The Hague. Come and run with us and enjoy the (almost) Spring weather before Spring actually arrives.  :-)\n\nI'm going to try to arrange a bag drop, but will not know until tomorrow. I can guarantee that we will end in a protected area and if the weather is really crap, we'll end at a pub.\n\nDetails:\n\nRun number: 187\nLocation: Den Haag, Laan van NOI train station (check Harrier Central for exact start point).\nRun fee: €5\nStart time: 1930\nBag drop: I'll try my best and let you know 24h in advance\nWalker's trail: Will not be officially laid, but I will send WhatsApp locations during the run.\nHare: Opee\nBeer: Good beer is ALWAYS available at FILTH Hashes!\n\nHope to see you there!\n\nOnOn!\n\nOpee","street":"Schenkkade 256, 2595 AW","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqfw002n1jhnih4ajjy6","description":"It's not a full moon or a new moon, but the FILTH couldn't pass up this once-in-a-lifetime chance to hash on 22-2-22. Please join us for a pub crawl in The Hague wearing your best tutu*. Don't forget to bring cash or a debit card on trail plus your Coronapass. Feel free to bring at least two friends and virgins--the more, the merrier.  We will also have a special celebration at 22:22:22 on 22-2-22!\n\nGuys, come meet Tula (depicted in the photo), and ladies, she has a brother (not in the photo, but also looks great in a Tutu!)\n\n*Tutus are optional but highly encouraged\n********************************************\nTime: Tuesday 22 February at 19:00\nHare: Opee\nLocation: Hague Humanity Hub, Fluwelen Burgwal 58, Den Haag, 2511CJ\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"58 Fluwelen Burgwal, 2511 CJ","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqk3002p1jhncx9a1hii","description":"We all need a good diversion from the bad news right now, so join us in Rotterdam for a pub crawl to celebrate the new moon. To test the intelligence of our group, we'll have separate starts times and locations for runners and walkers. If timing works out, we'll have an On-After option for dinner at a Chinese restaurant recommended by Just the Tip.\n********************************************\nRUNNER START\nTime: Saturday 5 March at 17:00\nLocation: Rotterdam CENTRAAL Station\nMeeting Point: Lockers\n\nWALKER START\nTime: Saturday 5 March at 18:00\nLocation: Rotterdam BLAAK Station\nMeeting Point: Outside of Markthal\n\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: NO--lockers should be available at Rotterdam Centraal","street":"Stationssingel 10, 3013AJ","cost":"€2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqok002r1jhnlgbjc63k","description":"Wear green as we celebrate the start of Spring and St Paddy’s Day.\n*****************************************\nTime: Friday 18 March at 19:30\nLocation: Hillegom Station \nHare: Give It a Blow\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqsu002t1jhnnt9glfh7","description":"Grab your bike and join us for this year's Easter Tulip Bash. The tulips aren't as colorful by moonlight, so we'll be starting earlier in the day. Please note that there will be no bag drop or guarantee that the tulips will be in full bloom. Hyacinths have already been spotted, so hopefully our timing will be perfect. \n\nLook for further details about a possible BBQ afterward. \n******************************************\nTime: Saturday 16 April at 14:30\nLocation: Hillegom Station\nHares: Give It a Blow + Start Me Up\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: No","street":"2e Loosterweg 2","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruqxf002v1jhnk4qyyz4l","description":"We'll miss the lunar eclipse by 14 hours, but that won't stop us from celebrating the super flower moon. The silence has spoken, so Opee is haring once again. Good news is that we can hope for an extra special circle since our former RA is visiting all the way from Hong Kong. \n\nNote: the start time has changed from the original announcement and there is no bag drop\n\n********************************************\nTime: Monday 16 May at 19:00\nLocation: City Side of Leiden Centraal\nHares: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: NO","street":"Stationsplein 3-B, 2312 AJ","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rur24002x1jhn3r6lrlc0","description":"It took 14 long years, but Lucy is finally getting his cherry popped! Come to this Dark Side of the Moon Hash to find out if DogShit is gentle with Lucy as he teaches this veteran hasher the tricks of being a good hare. We will meet and end at Lucy’s house in Scheveningen with a BBQ and gaming session. Bring your own food for the grill and booze (some beer and soft drinks will be provided).\n********************************************\nTime: Saturday 4 June at 15:00\nLocation: Aert van der Goesstraat 35, Den Haag\nHares: DogShit + Lucy\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"35 Aert van der Goesstraat, 2582 AJ","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rur71002z1jhn03tf7g3u","description":"You might have to wait to howl at the Super Full Moon until you're on your way home since we're nearing the longest day of the year, but that means there should be plenty of sunshine to help us find Opee's marks. \n\n********************************************\nTime: Tuesday 14 June at 19:30\nLocation: Station Den Haag Laan v NOI \nHares: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: YES","street":"Laan van Nieuw Oost- Indië 393, 2593BS","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rurbr00311jhn31nrc73e","description":"Brabant H3 will be joining us as we explore Rotterdam's bars further on this pub crawl (bring cash on trail). We have a time sensitive special feature planned with space for the first 20 hashers that RSVP on either FB or Harrier Central. Late stragglers can still follow trail, but might miss the special feature. No bag drop is planned, but you might be able to rent a locker. Meet in front of the station.\n\n**************************************\nTime: Saturday 25 June \nPack Gathers: 14:45\nPack Off: 15:00\nLocation: Rotterdam Centraal\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: No","street":"Stationssingel 10, 3013AJ","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rurfv00331jhnpdyvqirz","description":"Sorry for the delay--some of us have been busy destroying our livers at various nash hashes. Hopefully it's not too late for you to plan to join us as we invade The Hague H3. \n\nMeet at the parking lot behind the station (on the Voorburg side). Bring money along for the pub stop.\n**************************************\nTime: Wednesday 13 July at 19:00\nLocation: Den Haag Laan v NOI Station\nHare: Opee + XL\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"Laan van Nieuw Oost- Indië 393, 2593BS","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rurkn00351jhnqp21ma7f","description":"What a Great Day to be Gay (even if you aren't). \n\nCome celebrate freedom of choice, alternative lifestyles, our friends and families, and just having a good time at the FILTH / AH3 Annual \"A Great Day to be Gay!\" Hash event.\n\nThe day starts at 10:30 at Phillybuster and Hard Drive's house. From there, we will walk you to our private viewing point on the canals where you can drop your bags and enjoy a welcome drink before departing on a short(ish) Hash through the streets of Amsterdam. The trail will end back by the canal where our RA(s) will ensure you all have a chance to drink for your sins (past, present, and future).\n\nOnce the Hash formalities are done, enjoy music, food, and drink... and most importantly an unobstructed view of the Gay Pride Boat Parade.\n\nPlease note: THIS IS AN RSVP REQUIRED EVENT (sorry for shouting). Please RSVP before Wednesday, Aug 3rd at midnight in order to lock in both your discounted run / event fee of €10 and also your VIP spots along the boat parade route. If you do not RSVP we will not be able to guarantee you space in the tent or refreshments.\n\n======\n\nFILTH Run #197\nDate: Sat, Aug 6 10:30AM\nLocation: Phillybuster & Hard Drive's house at Brouwersgracht 72 in AMS\nBag Drop: Yes\nHare: Opee\nPartymakers: Phillybuster, Hard Drive & Pink Panter \nRun Fee: €10 with RSVP, €15 without RSVP\nRSVP: Required before midnight, Wed, Aug 3rd\n\n\nSpecial Notes: We recommend that you bring sunscreen in case there's not enough space under the tent for everyone.","street":"72 Brouwersgracht, 1013 GX","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rurp800371jhnry0jo87i","description":"We will meet in the parking lot on the Leiden side of the De Vink Train Station (the side with the restaurants and shops). There will be a runners trail, maybe with a split for for fast and slow/longer and shorter. And definitely short cuts for walkers. No flashlight is needed unless you are planning to get lost. Bring money/pinpas for beer stop and warm cloth for afterwards.\n\n*******************************************\nTime: Friday 12 August at 19:30\nLocation: De Vink Station in Leiden\nhttps://what3words.com/deny.drama.crystal\nHares: Tasty Piss\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":"Maria Austriapad, 2331","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruru400391jhnny0dbpr4","description":"Just in time to celebrate the 9th anniversary of the revival of the FILTH, it's time to head back to Overveen for the first time in three years. Definitely time to go back to discover more dunes, lakes and \"hills\" outside of Haarlem. \n\n******************************************\nTime: Saturday 10 September at 15:00\nLocation: Overveen Station \nHares: Give Me a Blow + Start Me Up\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruryh003b1jhntcngnzeq","description":"Why celebrate the FILTH’s 200th Hash just once when we can celebrate it all weekend long? You’ll want to dig out your favorite red dress for the first of our three events. Don’t forget that accessories help bring out the best of any outfit. We’ll meet at Opee’s old office where we can drop off our bags before starting our pub crawl. It’s Cocktail Week in The Hague, so we might visit some new bars that serve more than just beer. Opee also promises to provide at least one of his signature cocktails. Bring cash/card for drinks on trail. RSVPing by 5 October is REQUIRED for this trail.\n\n*****************************\nTime: Friday 7 October at 19:30\nLocation: Hague Humanity Hub\nFluwelen Burgwal 58, 2511 CJ Den Haag\nHare: Opee\nHash Cash: € 10 \nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Fluwelen Burgwal 58, 2511 CJ","cost":"€10","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rus2t003d1jhnf0me1wug","description":"The second of our three events takes place in the Venice of Holland: the beautiful university town of Leiden which has 69 bridges over the vast maze of canals. Not only will we cross over them, but under one as well. For those of you that don’t like 69, we promise alternative (shorter) options. There will also be a walker’s trail. Please note that some of the bridges have stairs and could be challenging for a pram. We are looking for a spot for dancing, so plan to hang out afterwards. Please be sure to RSVP.\r\n\r\n*****************************\r\nTime: Saturday 8 October at 15:00\r\nLocation: Leiden Central Station \r\nHare: Opee\r\nHash Cash: € 5 \r\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Stationsweg 1, 2312 AS","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rus7c003f1jhn4bhxpjge","description":"We’ll mix things up a bit for the last of the three events of our special 200th weekend: we’ll do a BASH (bike hash). The trail will be +/-  25km and will end at a park where we’ll enjoy a home-cooked Bubbly Brunch. Afterwards, it will be a 1.5km ride back to the train station where you can drop off your rental bike. \r\n\r\nRSVP for this run is required no later than Friday 7 October  so we can ensure we have enough drinks and food for everyone!\r\n\r\nYou’re welcome to bring your own bike, but for most of us it’ll be easier just to rent bikes. Bikes with back-pedal brakes are available at the station for € 4.15 (a local hasher will need to help out with the necessary OV-card). We advise opting for bikes with handbrakes instead, which are available for pick-up at the station for € 12 from Easy Fiets: https://www.easyfiets.nl/en/ (please note that everyone is responsible for pre-booking and paying for their own rental bike). \r\n\r\n*****************************\r\nTime: Sunday 9 October at 11:00\r\nLocation: Backside of Leiden Central Station \r\nHare: Start Me Up\r\nBrunch Chef: Opee\r\nHash Cash: € 10 + bike rental\r\nBag Drop: Yes\r\nRSVP: By 7 October","street":"Stationsplein 3-B, 2312 AJ","cost":"€10","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rusbn003h1jhncpr67j6c","description":"Brabant H3 will once again be joining us as we explore Rotterdam's bars further on this pub crawl (bring PIN/cash on trail). Technically, World Peace Through Beer is celebrated globally on 24 October, but why let the truth get in the way of a good Saturday hash.\n\nOpee promises virgin territory and fun & games at the end (which will be about a 15-minute walk from the station). There will be a runners' trail. Walkers will get inside information about the stops as there won't be a walkers' trail.\n\nNo bag drop is planned, but you might be able to rent a locker. Meet at the exit gates at the back of the station. https://w3w.co/limes.clashes.banana\n**************************************\nTime: Saturday 22 October\nPack Gathers: 16:00\nPack Off: 16:15\nLocation: Rotterdam Centraal\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: No","street":null,"cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rusg0003j1jhnanwxgmuy","description":"Just in time for Halloween, cum join the FILTH H3 as we partner up with Brussels Manneke Piss H3 for this year's version of the Zombie-less \"Zombie Run\": Ghost Train to Oblivion. \n \nUPDATE: There will be a separate trails for  runners and walkers with the runners visiting abandoned buildings as usual plus non-abandoned breweries and the walkers doing a brewery crawl. Sorry, but the runners' true trail is not baby jogger or dog friendly due to broken glass, although a shortcut can be arranged. \n\nHow to get there:\nPublic transport: Liege train station is a four-minute walk from trail start. \n\nWhere to stay overnight:\nIt's a bit of a hike from NL, so we recommend staying with us at Yust Liege, a new hostel with co-ed and female-only rooms. Of course, we hope Brussels hashers will want to stay and party with us as well. Book through https://www.booking.com or directly through the hostel: https://www.yust.com/liege/\n\nOn-After: To be determined, but will likely be a nearby pizza place\n\nTo ensure that we have adequate provisions, we kindly request that you RSVP no later than Wednesday 26 October via the Harrier Central App, Facebook or direct message to Tuna Melt. And please let us know if you're planning on staying overnight and joining us for the Hangover Hash on Sunday at 10:30 (a separate run will be posted). \n\n*****************************\nTime: Saturday 29 October at 15:00\nLocation: Yust Liege, Esplanade Simone Veil 2, 4000 Liège, Belgium\nHare: Opee + Give It a Blow\nHash Cash: € 10\nBag Drop: Yes\nRSVP: Required by 26 October","street":"Esplanade Simone Veil 2, 4000","cost":"€10","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruskl003l1jhnwcl9p4e8","description":"For those who stayed in Liege, there will be a Hangover Hash ending with bubbly and baked goods. Good news is that the clocks change so we get to sleep in an extra hour. \n\nYust has a nice kitchen for guests if you feel like bringing something to cook for breakfast. Don't forget to check out before trail starts; luggage storage is available for guests at Yust. \n\n*****************************\nTime: Sunday 30 October at 10:30\nLocation: Yust Liege, Esplanade Simone Veil 2, 4000 Liège, Belgium\nHare: Opee + Give It a Blow\nHash Cash: € 10\nBag Drop: Available at your own accommodation\nRSVP: Required by 26 October","street":"Esplanade Simone Veil 2, 4000","cost":"€2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rusp5003n1jhnex63riww","description":"If we're lucky, the unseasonably warm temps predicted on the day of our Hash will stick around into the evening. Regardless, the sunshine will be long gone, so don't forget a headlamp or flashlight and something warm for the circle. Last time at De Vink, we met at the Leiden side, but this time we'll mix things up and meet on the Voorschoten side.\n*****************************\nTime: Tuesday 8 November at 19:30\nLocation: De Vink Station on the Voorschoten side\nHare: Boar Whore\nHash Cash: € 5\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Trompplein","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rustz003p1jhn6taw5lxq","description":"Temperatures have definitely been dropping. For this Cold Moon Hash, Opee will attempt to find some warm Christmas lights around The Hague. Best of all, we'll have a warm On-In on this A-to-A hash. Walkers and runners are welcome. \n\n*****************************\nTime: Wednesday 7 December at 19:30\nLocation: Hague Humanity Hub\nFluwelen Burgwal 58, 2511 CJ Den Haag\nHare: Opee\nHash Cash: € 5\nBag Drop: Yes","street":"Fluwelen Burgwal 58, 2511 CJ","cost":"€5","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruszc003r1jhntdzhog87","description":"For this Wolf Moon Hash, let's howl at the moon while drinking hot toddies in the burbs. Don't forget your head torch. Best of all, we'll have a warm On-In on this A-to-B hash with an optional dinner afterwards. \n\nAnd for people who live far afield, you are welcome to stay over and crash on one of our many beds or couches. Please RSVP and let us know if you plan to stay for dinner and/or overnight. \n********************************\nTime: Saturday 7 January at 17:30\nLocation: Voorschoten Station\nHare: Opee\nBag Drop: Yes\nHash Cash: € 5\nDinner & Drinks Fee: € 10","street":"Stationsplein, 2252 TW","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rut3z003t1jhnm1n4vjdh","description":"FILTH is teaming up this month with Amsterdam H3 to celebrate Hard Drive's 59th birthday and Chinese New Year: Year of the Rabbit. Opee, our hare extraordinaire, will lay trail and Hard Drive is in charge of the party.\n\nTurns out that in addition to Hard Drive, Phillybuster and Tuna Melt were also born under the Year of the Rabbit. According to Chinese folklore, each animal is associated with certain personality traits. \"The Rabbit is said to be quiet, reserved, introspective and thoughtful.\" Clearly whoever wrote that hasn't met any of us three.\n\n********************************\nTime: Sunday 5 February at 15:00\nLocation: Chez Hard Drive + Phillybuster\nHare: Opee, Hard Drive\nBag Drop: Yes\nHash Cash: € 5","street":"72 Brouwersgracht, 1013 GX","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rut8j003v1jhnyik3suxf","description":"Thanks to Boar Whore, we will be able to howl at the Full Worm Moon together instead of on our own. We'll meet in the parking lot on the Leiden side of the De Vink train station (the side with the restaurants and shops). \n\n**************************************\nTime: Tuesday 7 March at 19:30\nLocation: De Vink Station\nHare: Boar Whore\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rutcq003x1jhnbeak6a37","description":"Amsterdam H3 will be joining us for 2023's first FILTHy Dark Side of the Moon. Clearly it won't be dark at 15:00, but we'll need light to explore this virgin territory that I like to refer to as an Architect's Wet Dream. This will be a true A-to-B Hash, so please arrive by public transportation as we will not be returning anywhere near the start. Unfortunately, this also means that there will not be a bag drop--so only bring what you can carry or be prepared to bribe walkers to help you. Speaking of walkers, there will be some trail laid and some shortcuts given via WhatsApp. \n\nPlease wear green in honor of St. Patrick's Day.\n\nThis trail is not pram-friendly due to stairs. It is possible with a baby jogger as long as the hasher feels comfortable running in a busy bike path in order to avoid some of the stairs. \n\n**************************************\nTime: Saturday 18 March at 15:00\nLocation: Diemen Station\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5\nBag drop: No","street":null,"cost":"€6","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruths003z1jhn1k1kjm28","description":"Let's head to the heart of the bulb district  in search of pink hyacinths just in time for the pink moon.\n**************************************\nTime: Thursday 6 April at 19:30\nLocation: Nieuw Vennep Station\nHare: Give It a Blow\nHash cash: € 5 \nBag drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rutmn00411jhn2hl0phsf","description":"Grab your bikes and head to Heiloo for a change of scenery for this year's Tulip Bash. \n\n**************************************\nTime: Saturday 22 April at 11:00\nLocation: Heiloo Station\nHare: Start Me Up + Moonshine\nHash cash: € 5 for trail + € 5 for lunch\nBag drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rutrl00431jhnvcb9xgkn","description":"Did you know that there's some excellent craft beers brewed in Rotterdam? Come discover for yourself at this brewery run. Expect a run that could be up to 20K. Walkers are welcome to join at the breweries, but will have to sort their own way combining walking and public transport between stops. Bring money on trail. Runners should also carry an OVcard as we'll metro back to the start.  \n\nTuna's out of town, so all bets are off about the weather. At least you can bet that Opee will pull off another excellent trail with some cool virgin territory.\n\n**************************************\nTime: Saturday 6 May at 14:00 (NOTE: Change in date)\nLocation: Rotterdam Centraal by the lockers\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5 \nBag drop: Lockers should be available","street":"Stationsplein 1, 3013 AJ","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rutwf00451jhnossfz39s","description":"The pack will be small but of poor quality. See you there.\n.\nWesterPark is the best park in the world. That is where the run is going to be. It's Pink's first FILTH trail. Don't disappoint him,  give him a reason to feel ashamed about.\n\n---- Details ----- \nRun - 215\nWhere - Amsterdam WesterPark\n - https://w3w.co/damage.lizards.lottery\nHare - Pink Panter\nDate - June 4th, 2022\nTime - 14:45 - Pack off at 15:00\nHash Cash - €5\nBag drop - probably not","street":"5 Westerpark, 1014 BX","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruu1300471jhnnump6fft","description":"We've been threatening to leave for years, but looks like it's finally going to happen. Here's your chance to show us how thrilled you are that this will be our last FILTH until at least Eurohash. \n\nAfter the circle there will be an optional picnic in the park. \n************************************\nTime: Saturday 17 June at 15:00 \nLocation: Duke of Oz\nHare: Opee\nHash cash: € 5 + € 5 for picnic\nBag drop: Yes","street":"2 Oude Singel, 2312 RA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruu5v00491jhnceffwnwv","description":"FILTH 217 - Live trail by Boar Whore for a Monday night.\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes!\n\nWear gray or black with a hint of colour to show how sad we are that Opee and Tuna are leaving.\n\nStart is about 5 min walk from central station, next to the Mercedes dealer. Bag drop will be there as well.","street":"80 Vondellaan, 2332 AH","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruuam004b1jhnx8ge6hrt","description":"Bag Drop: Yes\nHash Cash: Pay as you go\n\nLittle Sissy Pants Hasher Boy is going to send us on a run through his lovely city of Leiden. And since he's the biggest party hasher in the city, he will show us some of his favourite watering holes!\n\nHow much fuel do you need (or want) each run? You'll get to try it out today! We'll stop by 3 pubs along our longest 6km ever!","street":"Pelikaanstraat 64, 2312 DW","cost":null,"clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruuf3004d1jhnvk4dd8cf","description":"1 September is the Leiden Ladies Run. We will use their trail as our run. BUT, only Harriettes can run (5 or 10KM).\nREGISTER HERE: https://store.ticketing.cm.com/01H0HS2RF8MZQPM9QZC9V6RX5E/step/4bd8297d-b405-4e78-ae71-d360d219bff2\n\nThe Hashers will provide a wine stop for them, and for any other runners that want some, to promote the HHH.\n\nStart of the run is 19:30, about 5 min walk from our place (address in the event). So be earlier at our place for bag drop.\n\nFor the hashers, maybe we can go for a short run after the event, or we just dance with a speaker and call it trail.","street":"162 Rijndijk, 2331 AK","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruujk004f1jhnzmydtqzf","description":"Start Me Up and Give It A Blow are introducing us to virgin territory. We start at the parking of Station Halfweg-Zwanenburg. including bag drop. Circle probably in the park, we get your stuff there.\n\n______Details______\nWhere - Parking Station Halfweg-Zwanenburg\n  https://w3w.co/stable.locating.toffee\nWhen - 30 September, 2023\nTime - 1500 hrs\nHares - Start Me Up - Give It A Blow\nHash Cash - €5 probably\nBag Drop - Yes\n\nGood to know - There is a runners and a walkers trail - Perhaps circle not at the station, but in the park. Nearby","street":"1 Houtrakkerweg, 1165 MV","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruuo2004h1jhnif9ye5h3","description":"Tasty Piss will give us a nice trail on this day of Rugby World Cup finals!\n\nBag drop at the bar, afterwards optional dinner for the rugby finals.","street":"oude singel 2, 2312RA","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruutj004j1jhn6cm6bra1","description":"The only run #222 that the FILTH will ever do. More than 8 years till we have triple digits again!\n\nSomeone will run us around the bollenstreek. It's winter, so remember your lights!\n\nHash Cash: €5\nBag Drop: Yes","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruuy5004l1jhnjhwq24fg","description":"Recover from the eating and drinking of Christmas by coming for a run and then drinking some more! Virgin FILTH Hare Artsy Fartsy will lay trail for us in Leiden. Start is at the Ankerpark opposite the zijlpoort. Bag drop available.","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruv2s004n1jhnba1c0ikf","description":"Newly appointed \"Master Hare\" Sissypants will be leading us on a murderous deadly trail through Leiden. We were told there might be horror stories and serial killers involved!\n\nProbably good to bring lights!","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruv78004p1jhn9iqqy6db","description":"Opee and Tuna Melt are blowing through town just in time for the March full moon. After Hard Drive and Phillybuster generously offered to host, it didn’t take much convincing for Opee to volunteer to hare. Join us at Brouwersgracht 72-2, door on left, top bell.","street":"Brouwersgracht 72-2","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruvbu004r1jhnpgc48m5r","description":"Time for Tulips!\nStart Me Up and Give it a Blow will be hosting us in Nieuw-Vennep for a chance to maybe see a tulip or two. There will even be some visitors form out of town, so let's show them a good time!","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruvgd004t1jhnzgaozstq","description":"This Wednesday we will be joining The Hague Hash House Harriers for their run, since the full moon coincides! Hash Cash to be paid to Hague H3. Bag Drop provided! There's free parking available at this location near Westduinpark and the beach.","street":"Daal en Bergselaan 1B","cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruvky004v1jhnke1qiwvl","description":"Time to tunnel! Guaranteed virgin territory!\n\nTo celebrate the (soon) opening of the tunnel under Voorschoten, there is a fun run through the tunnel. After that day, the tunnel will only be open for cars. Perfect opportunity for a nice Hash trail!\n\nWe will meet (with bag drop) near the bus stop, and trail will take us to the start of the fun run, and then back. Get tickets for the tunnel festival and run here: https://rijnlandroute.nl/festival/sportdag/5km-funrun/\n\nBest dressed team can win a prize--the hash should be able to win that!","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3ruvq0004x1jhni3ctmm43","description":"It is going to by a FILTHy birthday run. Boar Whore turns 82, too old to organize his own event, hence......\nSchool`s Out For Summer thus Slippery has some time on her hands.","street":null,"cost":"€7","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
