{"id":"cmr3rvqii001h3mhn80ah5l9c","description":"Hare: Ring Mattress &amp; Blind Doug\n\nThe start will be at Curriehill Station at the regular\ntime of 11:30 unless there are scheduling/strike\nissues. There will be a drink stop enroute courtesy\nof the hares (Ring Mattress &amp; Blind Doug).\nThere will also be a pay as you go drink stop at\na pub &amp; we will finish at a pub for lunch &amp;\nrefreshments a short ride from a train station.","street":null,"cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvqmw001j3mhnjppeqw4e","description":"As usual, an A to B from Haymarket Station.  The On Inn has good beer and does pretty reasonable Pub Grub.  \n\nI (DMC) am the hare, so you know how good the trial will be:-)  \n\nThe trail is  between 15 and 20 miles.\nThere are \"a few hundred metres\" on \"busy roads\".  \nThe rest of the route is on traffic restricted roads, cycleways and footpaths.\n\nHowever, some of the surfaces have needed attention for decades!\nIn summer you could do the whole trail on a narrow slick tyres,\nBut right, there are some very muddy tracts, so you'd be a lot happier with something bigger and grippier.\n\nIf folk could let me know if you are coming, it would let me book the right number of places at the On Inn...","street":"Haymarket Terrace Haymarket Terrace, EH12 5EZ, EH12 5HD, EH12 5JZ, EH12 5LA","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvqr3001l3mhn1g5em9a5","description":"A to B trail.\n\nWill need chunky tyres.\n\nThere are trains from Edinburgh and Glasgow arriving around 11:00AM, so we'll set off just after them.","street":"High Station Road High Station Road, FK1 5RD","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvqw9001n3mhn89fb7617","description":"A to B, starting at Drem station (NOT Dunbar)\n\n\"Slick tyres will struggle for sure, a gravel/hybrid bike will be fine\"","street":null,"cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvr0g001p3mhn3ks1zwm2","description":"A to B from Haymarket station to an on inn doing food near a station convenient for everybody.\n\nA trail of two parts, each a bit over 10 miles, with lunch in the middle.\n\nAlmost all of the trail is on quiet residential or rural roads, or on traffic-free roads or off-road cycle routes/paths. Some of those paths are distinctly bumpy: road tyres will work, but you might prefer something wider/softer!","street":"2 Haymarket Terrace, EH12 5JZ","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvr4x001r3mhngfjhhyvf","description":"Beerspoke 43.\nHares are McPlod and Lost in Station.","street":"46 Wester Bankton, EH54 9DY","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvr9e001t3mhn42yt1bm1","description":"Hare is septic.\nIt's all very flat.  He says.","street":"3 Meeks Road, FK2 7EW","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvrdt001v3mhnydq1fvb7","description":"Work commitments mean we've lost our hare for this trail.\n\nSo we'll go for a hareless whizz along West Lothian's Shale Trail (see https://shaletrail.co.uk ) from West Calder to Winchburgh, and then in to Linlithgow for a pint. \n\nThat's a total of about 20 miles, with (hopefully!) no checks, but things to read and look at.\n\nEdinburgh folks note that the 10:26 from Waverley arrives in West Calder at 10:57","street":"Station Road, EH55 8BS","cost":"£30","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvri9001x3mhnygh9wr8k","description":"Meet at the North East corner of St. Andrew Square, which is about 350m from Waverley Station","street":null,"cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
