{"id":"cmr3rvs1200253mhn3en6s6qm","description":"Ooooooh!\nOur 50th outing!\n\nNote that we're starting later than usual -- at midday, not 11 o'clock -- to make it easier for folks who live Far Away...","street":"Mucklets Road Mucklets Road","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvsil002d3mhnje8bvfl0","description":"To avoid the problems of approaching winter and uncertain weather, this Beerspoke outing will be a simple RIDE along a pre-specified route from Prestonpans Station to central Edinburgh.\n\nShould be suitable for all bikes.\n\nHares are Used to be Nice and Pick Me Up","street":"Station Road South Station Road South","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvsmj002f3mhngii0snyv","description":"Not a trail, just a simple ride to get the season going.\n\nWe'll aim to set off PROMPTLY at 11:35.\n\nThere are trains arriving at Inverkeithing at 11:13, 11:21 and 11:28.  BUT to avoid overloading the bike space, please DON'T all aim to come on the 11:28!  I'm going to aim for the 11:13.\n\nMegasaurarse is coming on the ride, and has booked a tables in The Cambridge Bar in Edinburgh to watch the Scotland/France rugby match.  This starts at 2pm, and she would be happy to have folks from the ride join her group.  \n\nGoogle Maps says that the ride should take about an hour and a half, so we should be able to get there in good time.  \n\nIf you DO want to join her/us, please say so, and she will try to extend her booking.","street":"Inverkeithing Railway Station, KY11 1DA","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvsqw002h3mhnf205d34i","description":"Blind Doug is the hare!","street":null,"cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
{"id":"cmr3rvsw3002j3mhnih9846h2","description":"Assaulty Dog is the hare, and she says...\n\nLOCATION HAS CHANGED!!\n\nKiltWalk is using chunks of the canal path along the originally planned route,\nand so the route has changed.\n\nMeet Glasgow Queen Street rail station 11:15 for 11:30 start.\n\nRoute will be on tarmac cycle paths and small country roads. Mostly flat with short hills near start and end.\n\nThere will be one cafe stop and one beer stop so bring your usual payment methods.","street":"North Hanover Street, G1 2AF","cost":"£2","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
