{"id":"cmrvdq7pb000q04hz68zpjnz6","description":"Please come and join our hare for the day, Dr. Fingers, for a trip around Marple bridge and the surrounding area.\n\nMeet at 14:00 at the The Norfolk Arms, Marple Bridge, and we'll head out at 14:30 for approximately 10K/6 miles around the area. Dr. Fingers has just been on Safari so expect her to regale us all with tales of exotic animals and capers in far flung lands. I've seen some of the photos, it looks like an epic trip!\n\nThe pub is dog friendly, and there's generally plenty of room to park at Brabyns Brow car park (which is a very short walk to the pub). They serve  decent food too, so come along early and have some dinner before the hash. If you're posh you might call this meal something else - but you'd be wrong!\n\nThe closest station is Marple, which is only a 4 minute walk away.\n\nSubs: £3 for regulars, free for kids and first timers.","street":null,"cost":"£3","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
