{"id":"cmsze1qfc002204if0kk24taa","description":"Please join our hare Beer Sniffer for a jaunt around Levenshulme. \n\nWe're starting from The Sidings, a traditional Holts pub from the 1960's, sure to be the best decade as in 1966, far from being something to do with football, it was the year that both Madam Sin and Cwoardelia made their first entrance into the world.\n\nAnyway, ancient trivia aside, we'll meet from 14:00 for an on-out of 14:30. The trail is dog friendly and mainly urban. The beer is good in the pub but the food not really a thing, so scoff before you arrive.\n\nThe nearest station is Levenshulme, about half a mile away, and the nearest bus is the 192 station south stop. There's parking at the pub or on nearby streets.\n\nSubs: £3 for regulars, free for first timers, kids and canine companions.","street":null,"cost":"£3","clear_run":null,"old_title":null,"title":null,"clear_time":false},
